! Silicon, eight atoms, PAW, PBE: the gradient-corrected counterpart of si8-paw-1k.in.
!
! Same cell and cutoffs as si8-paw-1k.in with a PBE dataset in place of the LDA one, so
! the pair measures what a gradient correction costs where it costs most. On the grid it
! is four extra FFTs per iteration; on each PAW sphere it is a second pass over an angular
! quadrature that has itself grown from 28 directions to 45, with a radial derivative and
! a spherical divergence in it. That radial work is loops in Fortran and dispatches here,
! which is the shape of cost this codebase has repeatedly had to batch away.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav=1, celldm(1)=10.20, nat=8, ntyp=1,
    ecutwfc=20.0, ecutrho=160.0
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Si  28.086  Si.pbe-n-kjpaw_psl.0.1.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (alat)
 Si 0.00 0.00 0.00
 Si 0.00 0.50 0.50
 Si 0.50 0.00 0.50
 Si 0.50 0.50 0.00
 Si 0.25 0.25 0.25
 Si 0.25 0.75 0.75
 Si 0.75 0.25 0.75
 Si 0.75 0.75 0.25
K_POINTS
  1
   0.250000  0.250000  0.250000   1.00
